         kubeconfig_file: /path/to/kube/config
 ```
+
+### Kubernetes proxy listener
+
+`proxy_service.kube_listen_addr` enables the Kubernetes proxy and sets its
+listening address without requiring a nested `kubernetes` block:
+
+```yaml
+proxy_service:
+    kube_listen_addr: "0.0.0.0:8080"
+```
+
+The address accepts `host:port`. If the port is omitted, Teleport uses the
+Kubernetes proxy default port, `3026`.
+
+The nested `proxy_service.kubernetes` format shown above remains supported.
+Do not set `kube_listen_addr` together with `kubernetes.enabled: yes`; Teleport
+rejects that configuration because both settings enable the listener. If the
+legacy block explicitly sets `enabled: no`, `kube_listen_addr` still enables the
+listener. When `kubernetes.public_addr` is configured, Teleport advertises that
+address to clients in preference to the listening address.
